        "Babel",
        "Tanit"
      ],
      "comment": "Babel: Jeht and the Falcons",
      "content": "Babel took Jeht in as a 'half-outsider' after the girl came looking for her father Jebrael's old tribe, and favoured her above other Falcons. She used Jeht to assassinate the remaining elders by claiming they had betrayed the tribe. When Jeht refused to kill the Traveler, Babel offered her as a 'live sample' to the Fatui and told Jeht and the Traveler each that the other had turned traitor. Jeht, once the lie was exposed, killed her in front of the Tanit.",
